over ssh.\n   - A rule not where the reader looks is a rule that doesn't\n     exist.\n   - Batch-read law: never page through a data source one\n     window per request. Dump once, read the dump.\n\n* THE MEMORY PASS (at cycle end)\n\n1. STATE.md: what's in flight, what's next.\n2. JOURNAL.org: what you thought about it.\n3. DIGEST.md: update if anything durable changed.\n4. The question: what was said this cycle that must survive?\n   Say it back before the cycle dies. Unlogged words die.\n[t+07:26/60:00 c33/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_07nler9a","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/i.ar && grep -rn \"DIGEST\" emacs.d/iar-memory.el 2>/dev/null | head -10; ls emacs.d/*.el | head -20"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[18:40:24] emacs.d/init.el\n\n[t+07:28/60:00 c34/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_2fkiebf2","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/i.ar && ls emacs.d/ | head -30 && grep -rn \"read-memory-file-full\\|DIGEST\" emacs.d/iar-memory.el 2>/dev/null | head; find emacs.d -name \"*.el\" | xargs grep -ln \"read-memory-file-full\" 2>/dev/null"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[18:40:26] agents.d\naudit\nconfigs\neln-cache\nelpa\ngptel-fork\ninit.d\ninit.el\nmetaconfig\ntest\nemacs.d/init.d/agent/iar-prompt-assembly.el\nemacs.d/test/test-prompt-assembly.el\n\n[t+07:31/60:00 c35/300]"}]
